# Custom blocking entries appended to /etc/hosts by lib/hosts_write.sh.
#
# Kept as data rather than as a heredoc inside the script: at ~320 lines it was
# most of that file and pushed it over the repo-wide 250-line cap, and a plain
# hosts-format file is also easier to diff and to audit than a quoted heredoc.
# The content is byte-identical to the heredoc it replaces.
#
# Format is standard /etc/hosts: "0.0.0.0 domain" to block, "#" to comment.
# check_custom_entries_protection reads this same file to detect entries being
# removed, so edits here are what the anti-tamper guard is watching.

# Custom blocking entries
# YouTube
0.0.0.0 youtube.com
0.0.0.0 www.youtube.com
0.0.0.0 m.youtube.com
0.0.0.0 youtu.be
0.0.0.0 youtube-nocookie.com
0.0.0.0 www.youtube-nocookie.com
0.0.0.0 youtubei.googleapis.com
0.0.0.0 youtube.googleapis.com
0.0.0.0 yt3.ggpht.com
# Channel avatars and banners. Same role as yt3.ggpht.com, which was already
# here -- Google serves them from both hosts, so blocking one leaves the other
# resolving. Caught when the phone's DoT resolver was checked domain by domain
# against the 14 the focus policy names.
0.0.0.0 yt3.googleusercontent.com
0.0.0.0 ytimg.com
0.0.0.0 i.ytimg.com
0.0.0.0 s.ytimg.com
0.0.0.0 i9.ytimg.com
0.0.0.0 googlevideo.com
0.0.0.0 r1---sn-4g5e6nls.googlevideo.com
0.0.0.0 r1---sn-4g5lne7s.googlevideo.com

